id: fraud
name: Fraud
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Bluff
requiresSkill: bluff
requiresRanks: 2
sessionLimit: 1
timeCost: 4 Hours
# "Spread rumours and/or misinformation within an area of your choosing." What is spread, asked when it
# is used and named on the card.
asksTopic: true
topicLabel: Rumour
topicWord: spreading
# "The area affected by your Fraud varies based on your number of Skill Ranks in Bluff" - the most it can
# reach, read off their Ranks and named on the card.
areaSkill: bluff
area2: at most a single city
area4: a full country
area5: an entire planet
# The Check is rolled from the sheet, at the Difficulty the ARC picks there.
effectNote: makes a Bluff Skill Check against a Difficulty Category the ARC sets (rolled from the sheet) - won: the common people (and any NPCs the ARC decides) within that area believe it until it is proven false
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Four hours spreading rumours: a Bluff Check at the ARC's Difficulty, and the people of the area
  believe them until proven false - a city, a country at 4 Ranks, a planet at 5.
text: >
  Fraud: You pull the wool over the eyes of the unsuspecting sheep of your local area, leading them to
  believe that whatever you say is obviously true.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Bluff
  –Session Limit: 1
  –Time Cost: 4 Hours
  –Effect: Spread rumours and/or misinformation within an area of your choosing. Make a Skill Check
  (Bluff) against a Difficulty Category set by your ARC. If you win, the common people (and any NPCs
  decided by the ARC) within that area believe the rumours and/or misinformation you’ve supplied until
  proven to be false.

  The area affected by your Fraud varies based on your number of Skill Ranks in Bluff:

  At 2~3 Skill Ranks, at most you can affect a single city. At 4 Skill Ranks, you may be able to mislead
  a full country. At 5 Skill Ranks, even an entire planet may believe your lies.

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Bluff. The rumour is asked when it is used,
# and the card names it with the most its area can be for their Ranks in Bluff. Once the four hours are
# spent the card says the Check is owed - rolled from the sheet, at the Difficulty the ARC sets - and
# what winning does; who believes what is the ARC's.
